# Build output. WITHOUT THIS the context uploaded to ACR includes every bin/
# and obj/ in the solution -- tens of megabytes of DLLs that the image is
# about to rebuild from source anyway.
#
# The subtler cost is the layer cache. The Dockerfile copies .csproj files and
# restores BEFORE copying source, so an edit to a .cs file re-runs the build
# but not the restore. Local build output in the context defeats that: obj/
# changes on every local build, the copied layer's hash changes, and every
# deploy pays for a full restore it did not need.
**/bin/
**/obj/
**/TestResults/

# Tests are not in the image and must not be. They reference Testcontainers,
# which would look for a Docker daemon that does not exist inside a container.
tests/

# Local tooling and editor state.
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.user
*.suo

# Never in an image.
**/*.env
**/appsettings.Development.json
**/*.pfx
**/*.key
.git/
.gitignore
